=== Step 2: your choices ===
  [ok] model: Qwen3.8-Flash-Next (Unsloth)

  1) UD-IQ4_XS (recommended) ~4-bit i-quant (Unsloth Dynamic), between IQ3_S and UD-Q4_K_XL in quality; on a PC with less than ~80 GB of RAM part of its experts are read from the SSD; download 94 GB, keeps ~8 GB of its 60 GB of experts in RAM   <- needs 48 GB RAM, you have 30
  2) UD-Q4_K_XL (recommended) 4-bit (Unsloth Dynamic): K-quant experts, between UD-IQ4_XS and UD-Q5_K_XL in quality; download 111 GB, keeps ~8 GB of its 77 GB of experts in RAM   <- needs 48 GB RAM, you have 30
  3) UD-Q5_K_XL 5-bit (Unsloth Dynamic): Q5_K experts with Q8_0 downs, close to Q8_0 in quality; download 158 GB, keeps ~8 GB of its 98 GB of experts in RAM   <- needs 108 GB RAM, you have 30
  4) UD-Q6_K_XL 6-bit (Unsloth Dynamic): Q6_K experts with Q8_0 downs; download 169 GB, keeps ~8 GB of its 109 GB of experts in RAM   <- needs 118 GB RAM, you have 30
  5) Q8_0 8-bit, the reference quality (every expert Q8_0); for a 192 GB PC; download 188 GB, keeps ~8 GB of its 128 GB of experts in RAM   <- needs 136 GB RAM, you have 30
  [!]  UD-Q4_K_XL needs 48 GB of RAM or more; this PC has 30 GB: it would keep 8 GiB of its 71 GiB of experts in RAM and read the other 63 GiB from the SSD while it answers (single-digit tokens/s on most SSDs), and it may run out of RAM
  [!]  installing UD-Q4_K_XL with 30 GB of RAM, as you chose
  [!]  a 12 GiB RAM budget is more than setup recommends for this PC (8 GiB: the RAM less 24 GB for the OS, the engine and the file cache that reads the other experts). Kept as you chose: the engine clamps it to the RAM it finds free at start (less 4 GB), and the file cache gets less room - it may be slower, or run the PC out of RAM under load
  [ok] RAM budget: 12 GiB of UD-Q4_K_XL's experts in RAM, the rest read from the model files on the SSD
